{"name":"Ginninderra","hex":"#b3d5c0","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[],"entries":[{"title":"Ginninderra","blocks":[{"text":"Ginninderra is the name of the former agricultural lands surrendered to urban development on the western and north-western fringes of Canberra, the capital of Australia. Ginninderra corresponds with the watershed of Ginninderra Creek, which is now in part occupied by the Canberra districts of Belconnen and Gungahlin."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Ginninderrastore.jpg/330px-Ginninderrastore.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ginninderra","wikidata":"Q5563173"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Ginninderra_catchment.png/500px-Ginninderra_catchment.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Ginninderra_catchment.png/500px-Ginninderra_catchment.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ginninderra plain","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGinninderra_catchment.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7d/St_francis_Ginninderra.jpg/500px-St_francis_Ginninderra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7d/St_francis_Ginninderra.jpg/500px-St_francis_Ginninderra.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Former St Francis Church of Ginninderra c.2004","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASt_francis_Ginninderra.jpg"}],"sounds":{},"pictures":[{"title":"Eva Green (Headshot)","image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/59/Eva_Green_%28Headshot%29.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","ratio":0.6662198391420912,"link":"ht